cock"] " led the qualifying with 121. In the final he was clear thru 19 shots, but missed his 20th target, and was tied by Norway’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/117330"} "Tore Brovold"] ", who was clear in the final with 25. Hancock was only 19-years-old, shooting in his first major international, while Brovold had been bronze medalist at the 2006 World Championships. But in the shoot-off, Hancock prevailed, making four consecutive birds and winning when Brovold missed his fourth shot. The favorites in the event struggled. " [:a {:href "/athletes/93037"} "Georgios Akhilleos"] " of Greece, world-ranked #1 coming into Beijing, made the final, but finished only fifth. Defending champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/42936"} "Andrea Benelli"] " of Italy placed only 24th. The two other Olympic gold medalists competing, " [:a {:href "/athletes/42967"} "Ennio Falco"] " of Italy and " [:a {:href "/athletes/93172"} "Mykola Milchev"] " of Ukraine, gold medalists at Sydney 2000 and Atlanta 1996, finished 15th and 32nd respectively."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Preliminary Round"] [:th {} "Preliminary Shoot-Off 6-12"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {} "Final Shoot-Off 1/2"] [:th {} "Final Shoot-Off 3/4"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1763"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/117326"} "Vincent Hancock"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "121 (1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "145 (1)"] [:td {} "4 (1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1519"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/117330"} "Tore Brovold"]] [:t